# Line endings are a fact about bytes, not a preference, so they are decided here
# rather than by whatever `core.autocrlf` each machine happens to have. The kho has
# always been LF; this also makes the working copy LF, which is what every consumer
# of these files expects. -> agentco-notes/SESSIONS_MEMORY.md §7
#
# ⚠ A `.sh` checked out with CRLF becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the container answers
# "no such file or directory" about a file that is plainly there. That is the trap
# waiting for the Docker work on the backlog.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows reads these itself, and wants its own endings.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.nsi text eol=crlf
